1582
01:30:41.895 --> 01:30:43.192
so, please bear with me.

1583
01:30:44.606 --> 01:30:48.760
Doug and I have been through a lot together.
Happy times and sad.

1584
01:30:48.860 --> 01:30:50.095
When I was accepted into the priesthood,

1585
01:30:50.195 --> 01:30:52.597
Doug was there waiting for me
with a huge hug

1586
01:30:52.697 --> 01:30:55.100
and a Bible
that was signed by Cardinal Enders.

1587
01:30:55.200 --> 01:30:58.704
And when his parents, Merle and Irene,
passed, God rest their souls,

1588
01:30:59.371 --> 01:31:00.588
I cried as if they were my own.

1589
01:31:01.790 --> 01:31:06.717
You know, my grandmother once told me
that the true measure of friendship isn't...

1590
01:31:08.213 --> 01:31:10.557
Isn't how you feel about someone else.

1591
01:31:12.717 --> 01:31:16.062
It's about how they make you
feel about yourself.

1592
01:31:18.348 --> 01:31:19.474
And...

1593
01:31:20.684 --> 01:31:23.795
I can honestly say
that I've never had a friend

1594
01:31:23.895 --> 01:31:26.398
to make me feel the way
that you have, Doug.

1595
01:31:45.417 --> 01:31:47.044
I'm sorry.

1596
01:31:50.547 --> 01:31:54.097
When Doug called me
and told me that he wanted to propose,

1597
01:31:56.011 --> 01:31:59.857
I was nervous. I was probably
just as nervous as he was.

1598
01:32:01.016 --> 01:32:03.110
And I remember asking him,

1599
01:32:04.853 --> 01:32:06.947
"Are you sure she's 'the one'?"

1600
01:32:12.736 --> 01:32:13.737
Damn it.

1601
01:32:16.114 --> 01:32:18.242
- He told me he...
- Stop!

1602
01:32:20.618 --> 01:32:23.087
- What are you doing?
- Just stop.

1603
01:32:25.290 --> 01:32:26.792
I don't know.

1604
01:32:27.375 --> 01:32:28.672
Doug.

1605
01:32:33.131 --> 01:32:34.407
What are you doing, Doug?

1606
01:32:34.507 --> 01:32:37.135
Are you sure that you want
to go through with this?

1607
01:32:37.302 --> 01:32:39.304
Thanks, Jimmy. I've got it from here.

1608
01:32:41.347 --> 01:32:45.022
Hi. I've got something to say.

1609
01:32:45.935 --> 01:32:47.312
None of this is real.

1610
01:32:50.607 --> 01:32:51.779
What?

1611
01:32:52.859 --> 01:32:57.490
See, although the flowers are beautiful
and the salad dressing is great,

1612
01:32:57.822 --> 01:33:00.826
we're not married, Gretchen and I.

1613
01:33:01.159 --> 01:33:04.789
We can't be because my friend Bic
is not a priest.

1614
01:33:05.580 --> 01:33:06.898
Shit, here we go.

1615
01:33:06.998 --> 01:33:08.900
Yeah. In fact,
he's not even in the Army.

1616
01:33:09.000 --> 01:33:10.485
His real name is Jimmy,

1617
01:33:10.585 --> 01:33:14.239
and I hired him to be my best man
because I had no other options.

1618
01:33:14.339 --> 01:33:15.782
Same with all my groomsmen.

1619
01:33:15.882 --> 01:33:18.243
I actually don't even know
their real last names.

1620
01:33:18.343 --> 01:33:19.936
- Bronstein.
- ...is Japanese.

1621
01:33:20.095 --> 01:33:23.941
It's good to meet you guys.
So, please stay and enjoy the cake.

1622
01:33:26.017 --> 01:33:28.420
- What do we do now?
- We need to get the fuck out of here.

1623
01:33:28.520 --> 01:33:30.739
Yeah. Great stuff tonight.
Thank you so much, bud.

1624
01:33:31.356 --> 01:33:33.404
Are you out of your fucking mind?

1625
01:33:35.860 --> 01:33:37.262
Look, Gretch, who were we kidding?

1626
01:33:37.362 --> 01:33:39.097
You didn't grow up
dreaming of a guy like me.

1627
01:33:39.197 --> 01:33:41.666
Your knight is out there somewhere.
Go find him.

1628
01:33:41.825 --> 01:33:43.577
I'm going to tear your head off.

1629
01:33:43.827 --> 01:33:45.937
You goddamn motherfucking
pathetic piece of shit.

1630
01:33:46.037 --> 01:33:47.689
- Señor, let's just relax.
- Get out of my way, you fairy.

1631
01:33:47.789 --> 01:33:48.961
Fairy?

1632
01:33:52.168 --> 01:33:54.170
- Love you, Dougie!
- Calm down.

1633
01:33:54.462 --> 01:33:57.887
You motherfuckers! I swear to God...

1634
01:34:02.720 --> 01:34:04.893
What the fuck? I will cut you!

1635
01:34:05.640 --> 01:34:06.732
Shit, man.

1636
01:34:07.350 --> 01:34:10.024
Good game, kid.
That was a hell of a catch.

1637
01:34:11.187 --> 01:34:12.188
All right. Thanks.

1638
01:34:12.647 --> 01:34:14.758
Hey. No ass-touching off the field, Joe.

1639
01:34:14.858 --> 01:34:17.761
I knew you were full of shit
from the moment I met you.

1640
01:34:17.861 --> 01:34:19.846
I know this is gonna sound crazy,
but if you're ever in the mood,

1641
01:34:19.946 --> 01:34:21.264
I know a place that has great burritos.

1642
01:34:21.364 --> 01:34:23.767
You just ruined my sister's wedding
and you're asking me out on a date?

1643
01:34:23.867 --> 01:34:25.244
Yes, I am. Can I call you?

1644
01:34:26.911 --> 01:34:28.254
- Yeah, you better.
- I will.

1645
01:34:36.004 --> 01:34:39.178
- We were this close, Doug.
- Yeah, well, maybe next time.

1646
01:34:39.340 --> 01:34:40.341
Yeah.

1647
01:34:42.051 --> 01:34:43.052
Here.

1648
01:34:44.846 --> 01:34:48.191
- You saved me, Jimmy.
- Yeah, well, you saved me, too.

1649
01:34:48.433 --> 01:34:50.231
Did you mean what you said back there?

1650
01:34:51.603 --> 01:34:52.650
Am I really your friend?

1651
01:34:53.313 --> 01:34:54.690
Yeah, of course I meant it.

1652
01:34:56.441 --> 01:34:58.301
Does that mean you don't want my money?

1653
01:34:58.401 --> 01:35:00.637
Fuck yeah, I want this money.
I earned this money, man.

1654
01:35:00.737 --> 01:35:03.616
Damn it.
So, what the hell do we do now?

1655
01:35:03.781 --> 01:35:05.850
You still have those two first-class
tickets for your honeymoon?

1656
01:35:05.950 --> 01:35:07.793
- Yeah, why?
- I've got an idea.

1657
01:35:08.286 --> 01:35:10.709
This is going to be
the best honeymoon ever!

1658
01:35:11.581 --> 01:35:13.629
Ever honeymoon best
the be to going is this!

1659
01:35:13.958 --> 01:35:16.086
- Cheers, my friend.
- To your first guy trip.

1660
01:35:16.294 --> 01:35:17.466
I'll drink to that.

1661
01:35:18.796 --> 01:35:22.300
Everyone, please,
I need you to take your seats.

1662
01:35:22.467 --> 01:35:24.310
Please fasten your seat belts.

1663
01:35:24.928 --> 01:35:26.805
Can I unfasten my pants belt?

1664
01:35:30.183 --> 01:35:31.876
Hello. Would you mind
holding this for a second?

1665
01:35:31.976 --> 01:35:33.711
- Yes, Doug.
- Thank you so much.

1666
01:35:33.811 --> 01:35:35.279
No. Okay.

1667
01:35:41.486 --> 01:35:42.908
Hi, there!

1668
01:35:43.780 --> 01:35:45.828
You like that, don't you?

1669
01:35:46.115 --> 01:35:48.059
Is that a dog?
You can't have a dog on the plane.

1670
01:35:48.159 --> 01:35:50.728
- This? No, it's a service dog.
- That's a service dog, man.

1671
01:35:50.828 --> 01:35:52.080
Let me show you
what type of service it can do.

1672
01:35:52.413 --> 01:35:54.882
- Somebody send up the peanut butter!
- No! No peanut butter!

1673
01:35:55.166 --> 01:35:58.403
You put the weed in the coconut
You light that shit up

1674
01:35:58.503 --> 01:36:01.427
You put the weed in the coconut
And light that shit up

1675
01:36:01.589 --> 01:36:04.342
You put the weed in the coconut
And light that shit up

1676
01:36:04.676 --> 01:36:08.180
You put the weed in the coconut
And light that shit up

1677
01:36:08.429 --> 01:36:12.024
You put the weed in the coconut

1678
01:36:12.141 --> 01:36:14.460
And you light that shit up

1679
01:36:14.560 --> 01:36:16.654
Stop it, Doug.

1680
01:36:16.813 --> 01:36:18.690
I got a bad feeling about this flight.

1681
01:41:09.272 --> 01:41:10.774
- Okay. Yeah.
- Okay?

1682
01:41:10.940 --> 01:41:12.157
Put your weight into it.

1683
01:41:14.652 --> 01:41:16.370
You hit me in my back.

1684
01:41:16.988 --> 01:41:19.082
- I trust you, you're not gonna do it.
- Don't trust me!
